{"about": "Openings and details of single building walls as seen on site (street-level panoramas the player licensed, 2026-11), keyed by the building's identifier in the Hessian LoD2 models. Facts only - no pictures. A wall is named by its two ground corners a and b ([x, z] world metres, in the order of the LoD2 wall polygon, which runs left to right as seen from outside: the outward normal is (-(bz-az), bx-ax) normalised) and its base height y (the polygon's lowest point); the corners are rounded to 1 cm, so match them with a few cm of tolerance. Positions are in wall metres: u along a->b from a, v up from base. windows/doors/shopfront: [u0, v0, u1, v1]; balconies: [u0, u1, v, depth] (slab at height v, depth estimated); plinth: band at the foot {h, colour}. Walls not listed (hidden by trees, not seen, blurred) keep their procedural look; a listed wall with no windows was seen to have none.",
